<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!-- L shape in the x-y plane, 5 high in z, of 4 boxes of 5 x 5 x 5. The
     bounding box is 15 x 10 x 5 with its center at (17.5, 25, 32.5).
     Cells 0 to 2: three hexahedra along x (y 20 to 25): the west box
     (x 10 to 15), the middle box (x 15 to 20) and the east box (x 20 to 25).
     Cell 3: a hexahedron in +y of the west box (the north box, y 25 to 30).
     Regions: west_box = cell 0, east_box = cell 2, other_boxes = cells 1, 3.
     Cells 4 to 21: the outer faces as quads; the faces on one plane are one
     boundary surface:
       north (y = 30): cell 4, the end face of the north box
       east (x = 25): cell 5, the end face of the east box
       west (x = 10): cells 6, 7 (west box, north box)
       south (y = 20): cells 8 to 10 (west, middle, east box)
       inner_east (x = 15, y 25 to 30): cell 11 (north box, side to +x)
       inner_north (y = 25, x 15 to 25): cells 12, 13 (middle, east box,
         side to +y)
       bottom (z = 30): cells 14 to 17 (west, middle, east, north box)
       top (z = 35): cells 18 to 21 (west, middle, east, north box)
     north and east are first: a new shape makes them the in-flow and the
     out-flow. -->
<!-- Description: An L shape of four boxes of 5 m: the west, middle and east
     boxes along x, and the north box at +y of the west box; from
     (10, 20, 30) to (25, 30, 35). Regions: west_box, east_box and
     other_boxes (the middle and the north box). Each plane of the outer
     faces is a boundary surface: north (end face of the north box, y = 30),
     east (end face of the east box, x = 25), west (x = 10), south (y = 20),
     inner_east and inner_north (the two faces of the inner corner, x = 15
     and y = 25), bottom (z = 30) and top (z = 35). -->
